      "traceTextDiagram": "PR Comments Skill Processing Pipeline\n├── main() entry point \u003c-- 2a\n│   ├── ci_prcomments.New() \u003c-- 2b\n│   │   └── Skill struct initialization \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:45\n│   └── skill.Run(ctx, req) \u003c-- 2c\n│       ├── Run() method entry \u003c-- 2d\n│       │   ├── extractPRComments(ctx) call\n│       │   │   ├── getGitHubClient(ctx) setup \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:85\n│       │   │   │   └── GitHub API client creation \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:86\n│       │   │   ├── PullRequests.Get() call \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:92\n│       │   │   │   └── Fetch PR data from API \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:93\n│       │   │   └── Issues.ListComments() call \u003c-- 2e\n│       │   │       └── Extract PR comments \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:99\n│       │   └── Response formatting \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:75\n│       └── Error handling \u0026 return \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:70\n└── Skill framework integration \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:15\n    └── skill.Request/Response handling \u003c-- skills/ci_prcomments/main.go:32",
      "traceGuide": "# Motivation\n\nThe PR Comments skill solves the **critical need** for automated pull request analysis in CI/CD pipelines. When developers submit PRs, teams need to **extract and process comments** for code review insights, automated feedback, and quality checks. This skill automates what would otherwise be manual review processes, enabling **faster code reviews** and consistent feedback patterns.\n\n# Details\n\nThe skill starts with a standard Go entry point [2a] that creates a new skill instance [2b]. The core execution happens in the `Run()` method [2d], which orchestrates the entire PR comment extraction process. \n\nThe skill first establishes a **GitHub API client** [2e] to authenticate and communicate with GitHub's services. It then fetches the specific pull request data and retrieves all associated comments using GitHub's Issues API. The extracted comments are processed and formatted into a structured response that can be consumed by other parts of the foxctl system.\n\nThe implementation follows foxctl's skill framework pattern, with proper error handling and response formatting. The skill is designed to work within the broader foxctl ecosystem, where it can be invoked as part of automated workflows or CI pipelines."
    },
